			"date": "2022-11-17T03:30:47.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@brianleroux\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>brianleroux</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> WebdriverIO will ship with a browser runner in the upcoming major release that makes it finally very easy to render and test components in a real browser using standardized user interactions through the WebDriver protocol. All powered by Vite. Some examples can be found here: <a href=\"https://github.com/webdriverio/component-testing-examples\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">github.com/webdriverio/compone</span><span class=\"invisible\">nt-testing-examples</span></a></p>",
